    "created_at": "2016-07-13T19:48:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-13T19:48:53Z",
    "body": "Drive-by comment: The only outstanding security/privacy issue I can think of with canvas text rendering is that it can be used for fingerprinting. But that has more to do with local fonts than with cross-origin fonts (you can sniff which fonts are installed on the client OS).  I don't think we are about to start tainting canvases that use local fonts...\n",
